From: user <user@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wxQt iOS: dialog titlebar strip is a pure overlay (round 17, Job O)

Dialogs were missing their button rows (the symbol chooser showed
no OK/Cancel). Root cause, source-proven (round 17 Job O
forensics): this file's ensureTitleBar() dialog branch grew every
dialog by the 44 px strip height through a direct
QWidget::resize() and shifted its children down once. The resize
bypassed the universal clamp (wx 0017 hooks wx geometry requests
and wxTopLevelWindowQt::Show() only), and KiCad's grow-only size
persistence (DIALOG_SHIM::Show()'s max() restore; the chooser
panels' raw size saves) banked the +44 into settings on every
open -- dialogs are recreated per open, so the once-guard reset
each time. Height ratcheted +44 per open until the dialog pinned
at screen height through wx and screen height + 44 after the
grow, its bottom-anchored button row permanently off-screen.

Remove the grow-and-shift: the strip is installed as a pure
overlay, the state every dialog already reached in practice
because any wx relayout undid the shift (round 16's own comment
conceded this). With nothing grown, saved sizes stop ratcheting
and already-banked sizes self-heal through the clamp on the next
open -- no settings wipe, no KiCad-side change. The fix sits in
the app-wide event filter path, below every dialog class:
~170 DIALOG_SHIM dialogs, both choosers, PAGED_DIALOG, non-shim
wxDialogs and the wizard are all covered by construction; frames
(QMainWindow menu-host path) never had the grow and are
untouched. A wxLogTrace literal (jobo-titlebar-overlay-only)
marks the fixed path in the shipped binary; the grow expression
"host->height() + kTitleBarHeight" no longer exists anywhere in
the file.

Signed-off-by: user <user@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/src/qt/toplevel.cpp
+++ b/src/qt/toplevel.cpp
@@ -13,6 +13,10 @@
 // [KiCad-IOS port] Added 2026-11-09 for iOS (round 16, KiCad-V1):
 // wxQtIOSClampTopLevelRect() declaration for the Show() clamp below.
 #include "wx/qt/private/utils.h"
+// [KiCad-IOS port] Added 2026-11-09 for iOS (round 17, Jobs O
+// and P, wx patches 0024/0025): wxLogTrace for the round-17
+// traces in this file.
+#include "wx/log.h"
 #include <QtGui/QIcon>
 #include <QtWidgets/QWidget>
 #if defined( Q_OS_IOS )
@@ -550,7 +554,16 @@
 // amount, so the strip occupies newly created space rather
 // than covering content (a later wx relayout can only undo the
 // shift, returning that dialog to a plain top overlay).
-//
+// [KiCad-IOS port] Modified 2026-11-09 for iOS (round 17, Job O,
+// wx patch 0025): the grow-and-shift is GONE. The direct
+// QWidget::resize() bypassed the universal clamp (wx 0017 hooks
+// wx geometry requests and Show() only), and KiCad's grow-only
+// size persistence banked the +44 into settings on every open
+// -- a +44-per-open ratchet that ended with dialogs at screen
+// height + 44 and their button rows off-screen. Dialog strips
+// are now pure overlays from the start: the state every dialog
+// already reached after its first wx relayout undid the shift.
+
 // The implementation compiles only for iOS (Q_OS_IOS); other wxQt
 // builds get the empty stub at the bottom.
 // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
@@ -1476,26 +1489,31 @@
         }
         else
         {
-            // Dialogs and plain top-levels: no menu bar, no layout
-            // slot. Grow the window by the strip height and shift
-            // its existing children down by the same amount ONCE,
-            // so the overlay strip at the top occupies new space
-            // instead of covering the top row of content.
-            if ( !tb.shifted )
-            {
-                host->resize( host->width(),
-                              host->height() + kTitleBarHeight );
-                const QList<QObject *> children = host->children();
-                for ( QObject *obj : children )
-                {
-                    if ( QWidget *child = qobject_cast<QWidget *>( obj ) )
-                        child->move( child->x(),
-                                     child->y() + kTitleBarHeight );
-                }
-                tb.shifted = true;
-            }
+            // [KiCad-IOS port] Modified 2026-11-09 for iOS (round
+            // 17, Job O, wx patch 0025): dialogs and plain
+            // top-levels get the strip as a PURE OVERLAY. The
+            // round-16 grow-and-shift (resize the host by the
+            // strip height, shift children down once) is removed:
+            // the direct QWidget::resize() bypassed the universal
+            // clamp (wx 0017 hooks wx geometry requests and
+            // wxTopLevelWindowQt::Show() only, never this call),
+            // and KiCad's grow-only size persistence --
+            // DIALOG_SHIM::Show()'s max() restore and the chooser
+            // panels' raw saves -- banked the +44 into settings on
+            // every open, a +44-per-open ratchet ending with the
+            // dialog at screen height + 44 and its
+            // bottom-anchored button row off-screen (the symbol
+            // chooser's missing OK/Cancel). No top-level resize
+            // happens here any more; with nothing grown, saved
+            // sizes stop ratcheting and already-banked sizes
+            // self-heal through the clamp on the next open. The
+            // overlay trade is the one round 16 already accepted
+            // in practice: any wx relayout undid the shift anyway.
             if ( tb.strip->parentWidget() != host )
                 tb.strip->setParent( host );
+            wxLogTrace( "kicad-ios-round17",
+                        "jobo-titlebar-overlay-only: dialog strip "
+                        "installed without resize" );
             positionTitleBar( host );
         }
 
